**Plan ready. Nothing changed.**

One catch first. The table drops `owner` and `slow` on purpose, per the note in [format.js:3](src/format.js:3). So "same data" splits two ways. I would print the full `buildRows()` row, all six fields. Say the word if you want the four table columns instead.

Three small edits:

1. `src/format.js` — add `toJson(rows)` next to `toTable`, export it.
2. `src/cli.js` — parse `--json` from `argv`, pick the printer.
3. `src/cli.js` — update `USAGE` to `usage: cli.js report [--json]`.

```js
// format.js
function toJson(rows) { return JSON.stringify(rows, null, 2); }

// cli.js
const args = argv.slice(1);
if (args.some((a) => a !== '--json')) { /* usage, return 1 */ }
const print = args.includes('--json') ? toJson : toTable;
process.stdout.write(print(buildRows()) + '\n');
```

`buildRows` stays untouched. Output is an array of objects, one per run, still slowest first.

Next: say go, or pick the four-column shape.
